<title>SPAIN: Spain wages were 4.2 percent up in Q1.</title>
<headline>Spain wages were 4.2 percent up in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish average monthly wages rose 4.2 percent during the first quarter of 1997 over the same year-ago period, national statistics institute INE reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The statement said the average monthly wage was 201,857 peseta in the period.</p>
<p>The latest available inflation figure showed May CPI rose 1.5 percent year on year, after 1.7 percent in April.</p>
<p>It was 2.2 percent in March.  </p>
<p>			Monthly wage		increase as pct</p>
<p>    Industry	215,344 pta		  4.6</p>
<p>    Building	166,661 pta		  5.0</p>
<p>    Services	198,520 pta		  3.3</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
